<title>SINGAPORE: One in two Singaporeans may own pagers in 10 years.</title>
<headline>One in two Singaporeans may own pagers in 10 years.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Director-General of the Telecommunication of Singapore (TAS), Leong Keng Thai, said on Thursday penetration rates in the country for mobile telephones and pagers would continue to surge over the next decade.</p>
<p>Leong told a telecommunications conference that Singapore already had one of the world's highest usage rates of these devices.</p>
<p>He said that two years ago there were 8.45 mobile phones for every 100 people in Singapore and 28.5 pagers.</p>
</text>
